.repoql/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Session-local state written by the global hooks in ~/.claude/hooks/. Every one of
# these is regenerated per session and means nothing to anyone else's checkout.
#
# DELIBERATELY NARROW, NEVER A BLANKET `.claude/` RULE. `.claude/skills/` and
# `.claude/agents/` are project content in other repos here and stay tracked; a
# directory-wide ignore would silently hide them the day this repo grows one. Same
# convention as worktrees-challenge and serina-learning, and for the same reason.
.claude/.verified
.claude/.test-change
.claude/.session-tracker
.claude/.sid-*
.claude/.worklog.lock
.claude/.edit-count
.claude/session-journal.md
.claude/worklog.md

# Scratch mockups from the brainstorming skill's visual-companion server, never
# meant to be committed. NOT a blanket `.superpowers/` rule -- this repo already
# tracks .superpowers/verdict.json (the CI-checked READY-verdict record) across
# many prior commits, and a wider rule here would silently block ever adding a
# new file anywhere else under .superpowers/, same class of mistake the .claude/
# note above already warns against.
.superpowers/brainstorm/
